---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import PhonePreview from '../components/PhonePreview.astro';
import StoreLinks from '../components/StoreLinks.astro';
---
<Layout>
  <Nav />

  <!-- ================== HERO ================== -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <!-- A/B alternates for the hero H1 — swap the active <h1> below to test:
        <h1 class="display">There's <span class="rust">money</span> sitting in quotes you never followed up on.</h1>
        <h1 class="display">You sent the quote. Then it went quiet. That's <span class="rust">money</span> you already earned.</h1>
      -->
      <span class="tag"><span class="tag-dot"></span>Built for plumbers, electricians, landscapers &amp; contractors</span>
      <h1 class="display">Your quiet quotes are costing you <span class="rust">thousands.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Foremann writes every reply in your voice and nudges you when a
        conversation goes quiet. You tap send.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-ctas">
        <a href="https://app.foremann.app/signup?plan=starter" class="btn btn-primary">Get your business number</a>
        <a href="#how" class="btn btn-secondary">See how it works</a>
      </div>
      <StoreLinks />
      <div class="hero-note">From $49/mo · Cancel anytime · Setup in 5 minutes</div>
    </div>

    <div class="preview">
      <PhonePreview />
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    /* .display runs -0.035em tracking, which at hero size closes the word gap
       enough that adjacent short words can collide. Open the word space back
       up without touching the shared letterforms. */
    .hero h1 { word-spacing: 0.12em; }
  </style>

  <!-- ================== HOW IT WORKS ================== -->
  <section id="how">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">How it works</div>
        <h2 class="heading-xl">Set up in five minutes.<br />Win jobs the same day.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <h3>Pick a business number</h3>
          <p>We give you a local number. Your personal phone stops ringing for work.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <h3>Train it on your voice</h3>
          <p>Tell us your trade, your service area, the way you talk. Foremann learns so it never sounds like a robot.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <h3>Send replies in seconds</h3>
          <p>Every incoming text shows up with a draft ready. Tap edit or tap send.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================== FEATURES ================== -->
  <section class="ink-section" id="features">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">What Foremann does</div>
        <h2 class="heading-xl">It watches your quotes so you don't have to remember.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid">

        <!-- Get paid for the quotes you already sent -->
        <div class="card feat-card">
          <div class="num">Smart Follow-ups</div>
          <h3>Get paid for the quotes you already sent</h3>
          <div class="feat-visual">
            <div class="fv-bubble fv-out">Sent you the quote, let me know!</div>
            <div class="fv-gap">3 days · no reply</div>
            <div class="fv-ai">
              <span class="fv-ai-label">Follow-up ready</span>
              <span class="fv-ai-msg">Hey, wanted to check in on that quote. Any questions?</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>When you've texted a quote and heard nothing back, Foremann nudges you and writes the check-in. No more money sitting in forgotten threads.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Know who's texting before you read the thread -->
        <div class="card feat-card">
          <div class="num">AI Summaries</div>
          <h3>Know who's texting before you read the thread</h3>
          <div class="feat-visual">
            <div class="fv-sum-label">Client Summary</div>
            <div class="fv-sum-row">
              <span class="fv-sum-name">Tom Braxton</span>
            </div>
            <div class="fv-sum-text">Wants gutters cleaned before rain season. Quoted $180. Waiting on his schedule. Prefers weekend mornings.</div>
          </div>
          <p>Tap the summary at the top of a thread: who they are, what they want, what's next.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- The reply's already written. You just send it. -->
        <div class="card feat-card">
          <div class="num">AI Drafts</div>
          <h3>The reply's already written. You just send it.</h3>
          <div class="feat-visual">
            <div class="fv-bubble fv-in">Any chance you can do next Tuesday?</div>
            <div class="fv-ai">
              <span class="fv-ai-label">AI Draft</span>
              <span class="fv-ai-msg">Tuesday works. I can be there by 8. Does that work?</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Every text shows up with a draft already written in your voice. Tweak it if you want, then hit send.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* TESTIMONIALS hidden until we have real customer quotes with verified outcomes.
      Restore by uncommenting and replacing with real names, trades, locations, and
      preferably a dollar/job-count outcome per quote. See docs/MESSAGING_AUDIT.md.
  <section id="testimonials">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">What contractors are saying</div>
        <h2 class="heading-xl">Words from the field.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid testimonial-grid">
        ...
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  */}

  <!-- ================== PRICING ================== -->
  <section id="pricing">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Pricing</div>
        <h2 class="heading-xl">One flat price.<br />No surprises.</h2>
        <p class="lede">No annual contracts, no setup fees, no per-message charges. Cancel anytime.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="founding-banner" id="founding-offer">
        <div class="founding-banner-text">
          <strong>Founding rate: $39/month, locked in for life</strong> — limited to our first
          {' '}<span id="founding-cap">25</span> customers. After that, Starter is $49/month.
        </div>
        <div class="founding-banner-count" id="founding-count" hidden>
          <span id="founding-remaining">25</span> of <span id="founding-cap-2">25</span> spots left
        </div>
      </div>
      <script is:inline>
        (function () {
          fetch('https://app.foremann.app/api/v1/_meta/founding-status')
            .then(function (r) { return r.ok ? r.json() : null; })
            .then(function (data) {
              if (!data) return;
              var capEls = [document.getElementById('founding-cap'), document.getElementById('founding-cap-2')];
              capEls.forEach(function (el) { if (el) el.textContent = data.cap; });
              var remainingEl = document.getElementById('founding-remaining');
              if (remainingEl) remainingEl.textContent = data.remaining;
              var countEl = document.getElementById('founding-count');
              if (countEl) countEl.hidden = false;
              var bannerEl = document.getElementById('founding-offer');
              if (bannerEl && !data.available) bannerEl.hidden = true;
            })
            .catch(function () {
              // Offline or the endpoint's unreachable — the static "limited to our
              // first 25" copy above already stands on its own without a live count.
            });
        })();
      </script>

      <div class="pricing">
        <div class="price-card">
          <div class="price-name">Starter</div>
          <div class="price-persona">Running your own jobs.</div>
          <div>
            <span class="price-amount">$49</span>
            <span class="price-period">/ mo</span>
          </div>
          <div class="price-annual">Founding customers: $39/mo, locked in for life</div>
          <ul class="price-features">
            <li>One business number</li>
            <li>200 AI replies to incoming texts / month</li>
            <li>Follow-up nudges on quiet conversations (up to 100 / month)</li>
            <li>AI summaries of client threads, on tap</li>
            <li>Voicemail with transcript, summary and a drafted callback text</li>
            <li>Unlimited inbound SMS</li>
            <li>iPhone &amp; Android app</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="https://app.foremann.app/signup?plan=starter" class="btn btn-secondary price-cta">Get your business number</a>
        </div>

        <div class="price-card featured">
          <div class="price-badge">Most popular</div>
          <div class="price-name">Pro</div>
          <div class="price-persona">Busy enough that every lead counts.</div>
          <div>
            <span class="price-amount">$99</span>
            <span class="price-period">/ mo</span>
          </div>
          <ul class="price-features">
            <li>Everything in Starter</li>
            <li>600 AI replies to incoming texts / month</li>
            <li>Up to 200 follow-up nudges / month</li>
            <li>Priority support</li>
            <li>Lead-source integrations as they ship</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="https://app.foremann.app/signup?plan=pro" class="btn btn-primary price-cta">Get your business number</a>
        </div>

        {/* HIDDEN FOR LAUNCH — Crew tier. This Astro comment is stripped from the page
            source (not just visually hidden). Restore this card (and the matching grid
            columns in global.css + the Schema.org offer in Layout.astro) when bringing
            Crew back.
        <div class="price-card">
          <div class="price-name">Crew</div>
          <div class="price-persona">Add a partner, spouse, or dispatcher.</div>
          <div>
            <span class="price-amount">+$19</span>
            <span class="price-period">/ seat / mo</span>
          </div>
          <div class="price-annual">Add-on to your Pro plan</div>
          <ul class="price-features">
            <li>Each teammate gets their own login</li>
            <li>Reply on the same business number</li>
            <li>Shared draft history &amp; client view</li>
            <li>Add or remove seats anytime</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="https://app.foremann.app/signup?plan=team" class="btn btn-secondary price-cta">Get started</a>
        </div>
        */}
      </div>

      <!-- Example math only — never present as a claimed/real customer result. -->
      <div class="dollar-math">
        Say you send 15 quotes a month averaging $1,500, and a third go quiet.
        That's about $7,500 in quotes nobody chased. Win back just one and
        Foremann has paid for itself for years.
      </div>

      <div class="pricing-foot">No contracts · Cancel anytime</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================== FIRST FEW DAYS ================== -->
  <section id="first-days">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Getting started</div>
        <h2 class="heading-xl">What to expect in your first few days.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Your business line and your texting turn on at different times — here's why, and it's not a bug.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <h3>Voicemail works right away</h3>
          <p>The moment you sign up, callers can leave a voicemail. It's transcribed, summarized in a line or two, and lands in your conversation with that client with a callback text drafted for you to send. Ringing straight to your phone is coming soon.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <h3>Texting activates after a quick carrier check</h3>
          <p>US carriers require every business number to clear a one-time registration (called 10DLC) before it can send texts — AI drafts included. It's a carrier-wide rule, not a Foremann thing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <h3>We handle it, then tell you</h3>
          <p>Your registration is submitted automatically the moment you sign up. It usually clears in 3–7 business days, and we'll notify you the second texting is live.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================== FAQ ================== -->
  <section class="alt" id="faq">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">FAQs</div>
        <h2 class="heading-xl">Good questions deserve straight answers.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">What is Foremann?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Foremann is a business phone line with an AI that drafts replies to every client text in your voice. You review and hit send. It's built for plumbers, electricians, landscapers, HVAC techs, and contractors who run their own shop.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Who is Foremann for?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Anyone running their own jobs in the trades. Plumbers, electricians, landscapers, HVAC techs, roofers, painters, general contractors. If you've ever sent a quote and lost track of whether you followed up, Foremann is built for you.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Does the AI text my clients automatically?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>No. The AI writes a draft in your voice, including follow-ups (and review requests on Pro), and you read it, edit it if needed, and tap send. The one exception is optional: the after-hours auto-reply (off until you turn it on) sends a single short canned message when someone texts outside your business hours.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">What if I'm not good with technology?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>If you can text, you can use Foremann. Setup takes five minutes inside the app. Most contractors are sending drafts on day one.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Do I keep my current phone number?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Yes. You get a second business number. Foremann doesn't replace your personal number. Clients only have the business line. Your personal phone stays private and stays yours.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">What if the draft doesn't sound right?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Edit it before sending. It's a starting point, not an autopilot. The more you fill in your voice profile (how you talk, words you use, words you'd never say), the better the drafts get.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Does it work on iPhone and Android?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Yes, both. Foremann is live on the <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/foremann/id6773165667" target="_blank" rel="noopener">App Store</a> and on <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=app.foremann.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Play</a>. Download it, sign up, and your number is set up inside the app in about five minutes.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Does Foremann see quotes I send by email or in other software?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>No. Foremann doesn't read your quotes. It nudges you when your last text to a client gets no reply. If you quote by email, over the phone, or through other software, it has no way to know a quote was sent.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Why can't I text right away?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>US carriers require every business phone number to clear a one-time registration called 10DLC before it can send texts — that's true for every business texting platform, not just Foremann. Callers can leave you a voicemail the moment you sign up. Your registration is submitted automatically at signup and usually clears in 3–7 business days; we'll notify you the moment texting (including AI drafts) goes live.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">How long does setup take?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>About five minutes. Pick an area code, give us your trade, your service area, and a few examples of how you talk. You're answering texts the same day.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">What happens when I hit my monthly limit?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>You get a push notification at 80% so you're not surprised. If you hit the cap, AI drafting pauses. You can still send and receive texts normally. Upgrade anytime mid-month and the limit resets right away.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">How is Foremann different from Podium or an answering service?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Podium is a marketing tool built for big crews and runs $400+ a month. Phone answering services charge $200–$500 a month for someone else to talk to your clients. Foremann starts at $49 a month ($39 for our founding customers) and you stay in the conversation — the AI drafts the reply, you send it.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">What's coming next?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Ringing calls straight to your phone, then scheduling, quotes, and invoices. We started with texts because that's where contractors lose the most money right now.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Can I cancel anytime?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Yes. No contracts. Cancel from inside the app and your billing stops at the end of the current month.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

      </div>

